# Review: SequencerPlugin

The code covers almost all of the spec. `Score`, `Track`, `Sequence`, `Note` and `Instrument`
exist as schemas, and `ScoreArticle` composes `TrackList` and `SequenceGrid`. The article adds and
removes tracks (removal cascades to their sequences), mutes, toggles and paints notes, and plays
through a Tone.js `ScorePlayer` that skips muted tracks and loops. The spec's `Note.data` field is
missing. `Track.color` is `hue` in the code, and the default pitch range is A0 to C8 (21 to 108),
not 36 to 84. Playback loops over the score-level `loopStart`/`loopEnd` range. Without that range,
the visual playhead loops over the active sequence and the audio loops over the longest sequence.

Test coverage is the main gap. The only tests are `viewport.test.ts` (CellGrid hit-testing) and
`lead-sheet.test.ts` (the text format). No story has a play test, and no test runs a scenario, so
nearly every behaviour is `untested`.

Of 27 items: 0 done, 18 untested, 2 partial, 3 diverged, 4 missing.

